HST Office: Sheets flags numbers stored as text and converts them ("Chuyển thành số", owner request 2026-11-13).

Like the leading suite's error checking, a text cell whose text is a number gets a green triangle in its
top-left corner, and the cell cursor on one shows a warning button whose menu has "Số được lưu dưới dạng
văn bản" (title), "Chuyển thành số", "Trợ giúp về lỗi này", "Bỏ qua lỗi" and "Tùy chọn kiểm tra lỗi".

- sc/inc/hsttextnumberparse.hxx: the rules, pure C++ (tested alone). Separators come from the locale of
  the cell's number format, never guessed: vi-VN "1.234" is 1234, en-US "1.234" is 1.234, and a number
  in the other convention is not one. Sign, parentheses, trailing minus, "%", đ/₫/VND/VNĐ/đồng or the
  locale's currency, spaces (also no-break) as thousands groups and full-width digits are read. Codes
  stay text: leading zeros (phone, CCCD, tax code), more than 15 significant digits, "+" with 8 or more
  digits, exponents, dates.
- sc/source/core/tool/hsttextnumber.cxx: cell check (string and edit cells, not formatted as Text) and
  the format a General cell gets: percent, HST's VND format, the locale's currency, or thousands, with
  the text's decimals; other number formats are kept. hstignoredtextnumbers.cxx: "Bỏ qua lỗi" ranges
  of the document (ScDocument member), kept up to date by the ScUpdateRefHint the UNO ranges use.
- sc/source/ui/view/hsttextnumbermarks.cxx (ScOutputData): the triangle, drawn from the cell info of
  the painted area only, so a 100 000-row sheet costs the visible rows; not printed, not in LOK.
- hsttextnumberbutton.cxx/.ui (InterimItemWindow + MenuButton, as Writer's page break button),
  hsttextnumbergridwin.cxx (ScGridWindow): the button left of the cell cursor (right of it at the window
  edge), in the active pane, hidden while editing and in read-only documents; moved on cursor changes
  and after each paint (posted). Help opens help/bang-tinh-so-dang-van-ban.html of the offline guide
  next to Help/HelpRootURL; options open Tools ▸ Options ▸ Calc ▸ View.
- .uno:HstConvertTextToNumber (SID_HST_CONVERT_TEXT_TO_NUMBER, cell shell, hsttextnumberconvert.cxx):
  the selection, or the cell cursor, in one undo step (list action of SetValueCells runs and
  ApplyAttributes per format); disabled without such cells (looks at up to 5 000 cells). In the cell
  context menu (hidden when disabled), Data ▸ Calculate and Alt+Q (FeatureSearch.xcu of the HST
  extension). The ribbon button (btnHstConvertTextToNumber, Data tab ▸ Data Tools) is placed by the
  ribbon rework (hst-ribbon-ux-rework), not here.
- officecfg Calc.xcs Content/Display/HstNumberStoredAsText (default on), tpviewpage.ui/tpview.cxx
  checkbox; tabvwsh4.cxx repaints open sheets when it changes.
- vi messages.po (sc, officecfg UI.po): Vietnamese labels.
- solenv scalc.suppr: the warning button gets its accessible name in code (as Writer's page break button),
  so the a11y check suppresses it.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0); the new files are MPL-2.0.
Test: tests/unit/test_sheets_text_number_parse.py, tests/unit/test_sheets_text_to_number_patch.py.
